### Backend Service Port
PORT=8080
CI_PORT=8081
AUTH_PORT=8082

### Better Auth Configuration
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8082/auth
BETTER_AUTH_JWKS_URL=http://localhost:8082/auth/jwks
BETTER_AUTH_ISSUER=http://localhost:8082
BETTER_AUTH_AUDIENCE=http://localhost:8082

# dj-site (Next.js) base URL — single env var that defines the canonical
# frontend origin used by:
#   - `resolveCorsOrigin` (Express-level CORS `origin` for both apps,
#     BS#1107) — accepts a single origin or a comma-separated list; when
#     unset/empty, CORS FAILS CLOSED (no Access-Control-* headers served,
#     `[cors]` error logged at startup) in every NODE_ENV. No wildcard
#     fallback: `'*'` + `credentials: true` would let any web origin make
#     credentialed requests. The auth service falls back to
#     `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` before failing closed.
#   - `trustedOrigins` (CORS for auth endpoints) — falls back to
#     `http://localhost:3000` when both `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` and
#     `FRONTEND_SOURCE` are unset; no error on missing value
#   - `rewriteUrlForFrontend` (email-link host rewriting) — falls back to
#     `http://localhost:3000` only when FRONTEND_SOURCE is missing/empty;
#     parse errors on the FRONTEND_SOURCE value (e.g. whitespace-only,
#     missing scheme) cause it to leave the source URL untouched, so email
#     links keep their internal `better-auth-url` host. No error logged.
#   - `buildLoginPage` (OIDC `loginPage` target — the `oidcProvider` plugin
#     redirects unauthenticated users to `${FRONTEND_SOURCE}/login` and the
#     dj-site app resumes the flow on successful sign-in) — falls back to
#     `http://localhost:3000` ONLY when `NODE_ENV` is `development` or
#     `test`. For any other `NODE_ENV` value (including unset, `production`,
#     `staging`), missing/empty/whitespace-only/non-URL/non-http(s) values
#     THROW at module load. Silent localhost fallback in prod would redirect
#     every OIDC user to a host their browser cannot reach.
# Whitespace is trimmed; only the URL origin (scheme + host + port) is used
# by `buildLoginPage`, so paste-from-browser values with trailing
# paths/queries/fragments are normalized to the origin only.
FRONTEND_SOURCE=http://localhost:3000

### Public read-only CORS origins (WXYC/Backend-Service#2061) — BACKEND ONLY
# Comma-separated origins allowed to read the three anonymous flowsheet routes
# (GET /flowsheet, /flowsheet/search, /flowsheet/range) cross-origin WITHOUT
# credentials. The wxyc.org listener pages are a static export and must call
# api.wxyc.org from the browser; putting them in FRONTEND_SOURCE instead would
# hand the public web credentialed access to the whole API.
# Unset is a valid steady state — no origin gets the grant, nothing is logged,
# and every response is identical to the pre-#2061 behavior. `*` is dropped.
# Production: https://wxyc.org,https://www.wxyc.org
# PUBLIC_READ_ORIGINS=

### Account-setup invite token (WXYC/Backend-Service#1969)
# TTL (seconds) for the tokenized "set up your account" link sent to admin-
# provisioned DJs. Default 30 days (2592000) when unset. Long-lived on purpose:
# DJs act on the setup email hours-to-weeks after provisioning, so better-auth's
# 1-hour password-reset default locked them out. Genuine password resets keep
# the 1-hour default; only account setup uses this longer TTL. Safe at this
# length because every mint site revokes the DJ's earlier invites, so exactly
# one link is live at a time.
ACCOUNT_SETUP_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=2592000

### Auto-DJ service account (WXYC/Backend-Service#1644)
# Idempotent startup bootstrap in the auth service (`createAutoDjUser`) that
# mints the `auto-dj@wxyc.org` service account the auto-dj-orchestrator signs
# in as headlessly (POST /sign-in/email). Unlike a DJ invite, the orchestrator
# needs a KNOWN password, so the account is provisioned server-side with an
# explicit one.
#   - CREATE_AUTO_DJ_USER: gate, defaults OFF. Set to exactly "TRUE" (case-
#     sensitive) in staging + prod to mint the account on deploy. Leave unset
#     everywhere else so a stray deploy never tries to create it.
#   - AUTO_DJ_EMAIL: the service-account email (auto-dj@wxyc.org).
#   - AUTO_DJ_PASSWORD: per-environment deploy secret — NEVER committed. Staging
#     and prod MUST hold distinct values (a leaked staging secret must never be
#     a prod credential). The same value each env uses is handed to that
#     environment's orchestrator deploy.
# The account gets the `dj` MEMBER role only (least privilege — outside the
# admin-sync set, so global `user.role` stays null). Reuses DEFAULT_ORG_SLUG.
# Skip-if-exists creates but never updates: rotating AUTO_DJ_PASSWORD later is a
# separate manual path, not handled by this bootstrap.
# CREATE_AUTO_DJ_USER=TRUE
# AUTO_DJ_EMAIL=auto-dj@wxyc.org
# AUTO_DJ_PASSWORD=

